  "question": {
    "text": "A container contains a liquid with refractive index of 1.2 up to a height of 60 cm and another liquid having refractive index 1.6 is added to height H above first liquid. If viewed from above, the apparent shift in the position of bottom of container is 40 cm. The value of H is ______ cm.<br/>(Consider liquids are immisible)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "80",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0007_215f42e5b993.png\"/><br/>$y=$ apparent depth of bottom<br/>$\\frac{\\mathrm{y}}{1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{H}}{1.6}+\\frac{60}{1.2}$<br/>Shift $=40$<br/>$H+60-y=40$<br/>$\\mathrm{H}+60-\\frac{\\mathrm{H}}{1.6}-\\frac{60}{1.2}=40$<br/>$\\frac{6}{16} \\mathrm{H}=30$<br/>$\\mathrm{H}=80 \\mathrm{~cm}$"
  }
}